sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant W as TrackController (wayside)
    participant U as Program (user)
    participant V as Program (vital code)
    participant M as SwTrackController
    participant H as Central Harness
    participant TM as Track Model
    Note over W,V: Inside TrackController.scan (UC-09).
    W->>U: scan(image)
    U-->>W: return AUTH_n
    W->>V: scan(image + AUTH_n, SUGSPD_n_b)
    V->>V: scan internal: OUT_AUTH_n := AUTH_n AND NOT CLOSED_n AND NOT V_MOV_s
    V->>V: scan internal: OUT_SPD_n_b := SUGSPD_n_b clamped to the posted limit (V_GT_n)
    V-->>W: return OUT_AUTH_n, OUT_SPD_n_b, OUT_HALF_n
    loop each block in suggestions (encode_outputs)
        alt OUT_AUTH_n
            W->>W: encode_outputs internal: track_circuits[n] := (the clamped speed, halved if OUT_HALF_n, authority)
        else not
            W->>W: encode_outputs internal: track_circuits[n] := (0, 0)
        end
    end
    W-->>M: read track_circuits
    M->>M: _outputs internal: TrackCircuitCommand(*circuit), keyed by BlockKey
    M-->>H: return TrackModelOutputs.track_circuits
    H->>H: _finish_tick internal: next tick, inputs_for(): track_controller_to_track_model(...)
    H->>TM: STEP: track circuit commands
    Note right of TM: The train in the block gets them. A lower speed or authority is what brakes the train.
